apply_name(0x1006E6B0, 'CMoProcessor_ScratchMatrixOp', 'CORRECTED from an earlier name (Pool_AllocSlot) that undersold what this does. Full decompilation shows a self-contained operation, not a standalone allocator: borrows a scratch slot from the 32-slot pool (+0xA90 counter, +0xA10 array), calls a setup virtual method (offset 0x5C), calls Mat4x4_Multiply (offset 0x24) with the borrowed slot, then returns the slot to the pool before returning. STRUCTURAL RACE CONDITION: the counter/array read-modify-write is plain mov/inc/dec, zero synchronization (no lock prefix, no mutex). Reachability from multiple threads not confirmed either way -- this codebase is confirmed NOT naively single-threaded elsewhere (sqmoChannelBuildSQO uses a real mutex, see the dancer middleware document), so this is a genuine open question, not purely theoretical.', True)
