apply_name(0x10237710, 'StAvatarCoordinator_StateHandler', "THE CONFIRMED REAL ENTRY POINT for the whole St*/dancer investigation. Slot 6 (offset 0x18) of g_pStAvatarCoordinator_vtbl. A switch over 9 numbered states; state 9 calls into the chain leading to StAvatar_Teardown/StAvatar_ReleaseResources. This is the real seam between FFXI's own game bootstrap and the dancer middleware's StAvatar layer. Located via search_bytes for this address's raw bytes, after fixing two real plugin bugs that were blocking that search (a missing 'import ida_idaapi', and a silent-exception-swallowing bug in the tool-call wrapper that made the first bug undiagnosable for two prior sessions).", True)
apply_name(0x1024D180, 'StAvatar_Teardown', 'Calls StAvatar_ReleaseResources plus ~9 other cleanup sub-functions -- the larger orchestrating teardown method. One callee (StAvatar_SwitchMusicTask) breaks the pattern of staying within the dancer address range, a real cross-connection to CYyMusicLoadTask.', True)
apply_name(0x1024D2C0, 'StAvatar_ReleaseResources', 'Confirmed real StAvatar method via two sqFree() calls tagged with StAvatar.cpp line numbers (352, 359) -- D:\\build0001\\FFXi_Win\\Main\\dancer\\StAvatar.cpp.', True)
apply_name(0x10250E10, 'StChannel_AllocFromPool', "Polls the dedicated 11MB 'Dancer' memory pool with a wait-and-retry (Sleep(2) once, then give up), then allocates from it. Tagged with the real .chn file extension (aChnFile).", True)
apply_name(0x10250EC0, 'StChannelItemAssignBuffer', "Frees the buffer if already loaded (flag bit 0x20) or given invalid size; otherwise assigns the new buffer and marks 'owns data' (flag bit 4).", True)
apply_name(0x10250F10, 'StChannelItemResolve', "Real name matching the confirmed error string 'StChannelItemResolve(): called with missing data'. Calls sqmoChannelBuildSQO under mutex protection (sub_101C4D30/40 bracketing), auto-upgrades an old format-version tag on success, frees the raw buffer via sqFree.", True)
apply_name(0x102512B0, 'StChannelItemClear', "Matches the StModelItemClear naming pattern. Checks a 'valid' flag, dispatches cleanup based on whether the item was built via sqmoChannelBuildSQO (calls its own release) or just holds a raw loaded buffer (frees it directly via sqFree). Called repeatedly inside StAvatar_ReleaseResources's array-clearing loops.", True)
apply_name(0x102524E0, 'StModelItemClear', "Real function name from its own embedded (dead/no-op) debug-print strings: 'StModelItemClear(A): called with non-NULL dmbPtr/dmpPtr [%p]'. Releases dmbPtr/dmpPtr (Dynamic Model Buffer/Pack pointers) via sqFree with file+line tags from StModel.cpp.", True)
apply_name(0x10252CC0, 'StTrigger_ProcessOpcodesUpToTime', "MAJOR FINDING, directly relevant to this project's VFX-restoration goal: the real opcode dispatch/execute function. Confirms opcodes are TIME-KEYED -- processes every opcode whose time has passed since the last call in one 'catch up' pass, matching a cue-track/timeline metaphor exactly. Confirmed type dispatch: type 0 resolves a named/numbered resource via the same resource ID (61) and resolve call already confirmed for SetMusicTrackVolume_A/B/C, then calls the identical function used there on success -- strongly suggests type 0 triggers a sound effect/music cue by numbered ID, with a spatial-parameter fallback path on a name mismatch. Types 1 and 2 write into offsets of dword_10455C20 (45 xrefs across nearly the whole .text section) and set a dirty flag. CORRECTED, not left standing: checking this object directly found it's allocated/freed at the CApp (top-level application) level and one of its own nearby fields (byte_10455C34, +20) controls gamepad input config, not camera/effects -- revises the earlier 'plausibly camera-shake/screen-flash' guess downward. It's better understood as a broad, generic app-settings singleton, not a dedicated effects structure. What actually happens at +3508/+3516 remains genuinely unconfirmed. Only types 0/1/2 were confirmed; other opcode type values may exist unchecked.", True)
apply_name(0x10252F00, 'StTrigger_RegisterCallbacks', "DEFINITIVE CONFIRMATION: explicitly registers StTriggerItemResolve and StTrigger_BuildFromFXT as a resolve/build callback pair in FFXI's generic resource-callback system (the same dword_10662DCC table used elsewhere), for the trigger/FXT resource type. Own error string confirms the term directly: 'Trigger file not found'.", True)
