apply_name(0x1026E1F0, 'sqxfXformTD_Update', "FULLY DECODED by disassembling the raw, previously-unanalyzed bytes directly (this address was never auto-analyzed as a function by IDA). Takes only 'this' -- no time argument, so 'TD' is not 'time-driven'; the math matches 'target/distance' better, though that expansion is a reading, not a confirmed name. Converts the object's quaternion to a 3x3 rotation and writes a 4x4 matrix (+0x1C-+0x58) whose translation is position + scalar x (rotation's third column): a boom/orbit placement, 'scalar' units along the object's own forward axis from a pivot. Used for both lights and cameras via a real code-generation template.", True)
apply_name(0x1028A040, 'sqxfXformMPrint', 'Confirms sqxfXformM is a simple static matrix transform -- just an embedded matrix, nothing else. Contrasts with sqxfXformTD (see sqxfXformTD_Create/Update below), whose Update was originally unreached (its .text region was never auto-analyzed as a function) but has since been fully decoded by disassembling the raw bytes directly.', True)
