apply_name(0x1028A800, 'sqgxContext_BatchIndices', 'MAJOR PERFORMANCE-RELEVANT FINDING: a real index-buffer batching/accumulation system. Accumulates indices from multiple shapes/draw calls into a shared buffer, capping batches at exactly 1000 indices before flushing. Includes correct degenerate-triangle-index insertion to bridge between triangle-strip segments when batching multiple strips together, plus a redundancy check that skips re-setup when consecutive calls reuse the same index source. A genuine, confirmed, already-implemented draw-call-batching optimization -- this submission layer is not a naive one-draw-call-per-shape implementation.', True)
apply_name(0x1028D770, 'sqcoConnectorPrint', "Resolves sqConstraint's real role: NOT a physics/IK constraint. Real, confirmed fields: active, source, destination, numCopyBytes, execFn (a custom function pointer), userData. A generic data-flow connector -- very plausibly the real wiring mechanism behind sqmdModel's Updaters array, propagating a computed value into another object's field every frame via raw byte copy or a custom function.", True)
apply_name(0x1028D910, 'sqmoMotion_Dispatch', "Real, complete type taxonomy confirmed via magic-number dispatch and matching error strings: 327681=FrameChannel (confirmed via sqmoFrameChannel_GetFramePtr's own error string), 327683=KeyChannel (by elimination), 327684=generic 'channel motion' (confirmed via sqmoMixerMotion_Sample's own error string), 327687=MixerMotion. The real, complete motion-type system underlying CYyMotionQue/CYyMoveBlendQue.", True)
apply_name(0x1028E3B0, 'sqsnScenePrint', "UNPLANNED CAPSTONE FINDING for sqScene, found while tracing sqrdCamera's callers. Reveals the complete real scene graph structure: numCameras/cameras[] (12-byte records), idCamera, numLights/lights[] (12-byte records), shadowOn/shadowSize/numShadows/shadows[] (48-byte records: type [0/1=Projected variants, 2=Volume], light index, numObjects, objects[], blurSize, stencil offset, shadow camera check, shadow volume extend -- the last directly matches a field already seen in sqgxContext_Dump), numLayers/layers[] (each layer: numObjects, objects[] as 144-byte records: obj ptr, mat ptr, shader ptr, lights). The real top-level scene organization tying cameras/lights/shadows/render-objects together.", True)
