apply_name(0x1029A420, 'sqskSkeleton_GetNodeByIndex', "CORRECTED from an initial name (sqskSkeleton_GetJointByIndex) that was wrong -- caught by cross-checking against sqskSkeleton_Dump's own confirmed code immediately after naming. Resolves into the NODE array, not the joint array: sqskSkeleton_Dump confirms the joint array lives at field offset 36 (156-byte stride) while the node array lives at offset 32; this function reads its base from offset 32. Its 248-byte stride is consistent with a node being a larger structure that likely wraps a joint plus hierarchy/parent-child linkage, though that composition isn't confirmed, only consistent with the offset/stride evidence. Called from sqinSkinBuildBinary while resolving a cluster's bone reference -- meaning a skin cluster's bone reference resolves to a scene NODE, not a raw joint directly.", True)
apply_name(0x1029ABD0, 'sqinSkinBuildBinary', "Real, complete binary parser building a skin's cluster array from raw file data -- name matches its own error strings exactly. Checks version==2, reads clusterCount and idMax, then for each cluster reads a bone-ID array and a matching weight array, resolves a bone/node reference, and calls sqinCluster_Create() directly, populating fields that land exactly on sqinCluster_Dump's confirmed offsets (the resolved reference lands precisely at the confirmed jointNode field). The same (bone_index, weight) pair structure confirmed by hand in SkinVertices many sessions ago, now independently confirmed from the file-loading side.", True)
